messages:
maria: quick FYI — I opened a terraform PR that updates the karpenter provisioner + PDBs for inference pools. Need a quick pair-on maxUnavailable & HPA interplay before canary. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/pull/482

jonathan: looking. CI shows plan OK. what's the current maxUnavailable?

maria: snippet:
```hcl
resource "kubernetes_pod_disruption_budget" "inference_pool" {
  metadata { name = "inference-pdb" }
  spec {
    maxUnavailable = 2
    selector { match_labels = { app = "inference" } }
  }
}

resource "karpenter_provisioner" "inference" {
  spec {
    ttlSecondsUntilExpired = 3600
    consolidation { enabled = true }
    limits { resources { cpu = "2000" } }
    provider { instanceProfile = "inference-profile" }
  }
}
```

ryan: if we set maxUnavailable=2 and have low replicas (3), we can lose capacity during upgrades. for critical pools keep maxUnavailable=1. also add `minAvailable` or follow our pattern to prefer `minAvailable` over large maxUnavailable.

jonathan: HPA uses CPU target 60% for batch-worker; VPA is enabled in recommend mode — should be fine. but confirm deployment strategy: set `maxSurge=1` and `strategy: RollingUpdate` so we don't drop too many pods at once.

maria: good catch. I'll change to `maxUnavailable = 1` and add `deployment.spec.strategy.rollingUpdate.maxSurge = 1`. also adding a canary label `autoscale-canary=true` to the staging namespace.

devops-bot: terraform plan completed — no drift. 2 resources to change. Plan summary: +1 karpenter_provisioner, ~1 kubernetes_pod_disruption_budget.

jonathan: also check the secret path for the metrics adapter — the PR references `vault://k8s/metrics` but our cluster sync expects `vault://platform/metrics`. that'll fail on apply.

maria: thanks — fixed vault path in PR, pushed commit. also added a short runbook note in the PR: `if canary fails, revert using infra/rollbacks/fast-revert.sh`.

ryan: LGTM after that patch. please run a dry-run canary in staging and ping me.

maria: will do. kicking off canary deploy in staging now — status: deploy-bot shows rollout started. will update thread.

deploy-bot: Canary rollout started for inference provisioner (staging). Pods launched: 1/1 ready. observed scaling: 0 -> 2 during warm-up.

maria: staging looks healthy after 10m. no eviction logs and metrics adapter is reporting. will promote to prod canary tonight 02:00 UTC. tagging @jonathan @ryan

jonathan: :thumbsup: add a one-line note to release notes about possible short-lived throttling during initial warm-up.

maria: done. merging after 02:00 canary window if green. thanks all.
